  <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem;">
    By <a href="/en/urban-gavelin/" rel="author">Urban Gavelin</a>, <time datetime="2026-04-21">April 21, 2026</time>, AI in Sales
  </p>
  <h1>From Hours to Minutes: Meet Your New AI Sales Assistant</h1>
  <img src={coverImage} alt="From Hours to Minutes: Meet Your New AI Sales Assistant" width="1280" height="720" class="hero-img" />
  <p class="lead"><strong>AI is no longer a future topic for B2B sales, it's already redesigning how proposals are written, how prospects are identified, and how sellers spend their time.</strong> Companies using AI-augmented sales workflows are compressing hours of preparation into minutes, freeing up cognitive bandwidth for what actually drives revenue: better conversations, sharper thinking, and faster decisions.</p>

  <div class="section" style="background:#f8f8f8; padding:1.5rem; border-radius:4px; margin-bottom:2rem;">
    <p style="margin:0 0 0.75rem; font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--color-text-muted); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.05em;">AI in sales, the numbers</p>
    <ul style="margin:0; padding-left:1.25rem;">
      <li>Sales reps spend only 28% of their time on actual selling, the rest goes to administrative tasks, tool-switching, and preparation that AI can now handle. <em>(<a href="https://www.salesforce.com/resources/research-reports/state-of-sales/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Salesforce State of Sales</a>)</em></li>
      <li>AI-powered sales tools reduce time spent on non-selling tasks by up to 40%, according to early adopter reports. <em>(<a href="https://www.mckinsey.com/capabilities/growth-marketing-and-sales/our-insights/the-future-of-sales" target="_blank" rel="noopener">McKinsey</a>)</em></li>
      <li>High-performing sales teams are 2.8× more likely to use AI tools than underperforming teams. <em>(<a href="https://www.salesforce.com/resources/research-reports/state-of-sales/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Salesforce</a>)</em></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <p>And I thought: this is going to change how we sell. Faster than most people realise.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>The shift is already here</h2>
    <p>We hosted a webinar with Mikael Wällstedt where we explored one simple idea: AI isn't just improving sales, it's redesigning it. Not someday. This year.</p>
    <p>Inside that session, we showed three real applications already in motion:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Proposals generated in minutes instead of hours</li>
      <li>Prospecting done continuously in the background</li>
      <li>And something I want to focus on today, because this one is different</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>Meet PA Uno, your AI personal assistant</h2>
    <p>This is not another tool. Think of it as a personal assistant, a researcher, a content creator and a coordinator, working for you, in parallel, all the time.</p>

    <h3>What Uno actually does</h3>
    <p>Imagine starting your day and instead of sorting emails, preparing meeting notes, researching prospects and writing follow-ups, you simply review what's already been done.</p>
    <p>Because Uno has:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Drafted your emails in your tone</li>
      <li>Prepared insights on your next meeting</li>
      <li>Summarised key accounts</li>
      <li>Generated reports and analysis</li>
    </ul>
    <p>And yes, it can be trained to sound like you. Not the robotic version of you. The real one.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>Why this matters more than you think</h2>
    <p>Here's what most people get wrong about AI: they think it's about efficiency. It's not. It's about freeing up your cognitive bandwidth.</p>
    <p>Because when you remove the busy work, you create space for better conversations, better thinking and better decisions. And that's where real sales happen.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>What we saw in the webinar</h2>
    <p>Together with Mikael, we demonstrated how proposals can go from hours to five minutes, how AI can identify new prospects every week automatically, and how entire sales workflows can be supported by intelligent agents.</p>
    <p>But something became very clear: the companies winning right now are not the ones with the best tools. They're the ones testing, adapting and learning faster than everyone else.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>One thought to take with you</h2>
    <p>AI will not replace consultants. But consultants who use AI will replace those who don't.</p>
    <p>The biggest risk right now isn't using AI wrong. It's not using it at all.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>Frequently asked questions about AI in B2B sales</h2>
    <div itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">

      <div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        <h3 itemprop="name">How is AI changing B2B sales right now?</h3>
        <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
          <p itemprop="text">AI is compressing work that previously took hours, proposal writing, prospect research, meeting preparation, follow-up drafting, into minutes. More importantly, it's freeing up the cognitive bandwidth that salespeople previously spent on administration, redirecting it toward higher-value activities: better customer conversations, sharper qualification, and faster decisions.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        <h3 itemprop="name">Will AI replace B2B salespeople?</h3>
        <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
          <p itemprop="text">AI will not replace salespeople, but salespeople who use AI will replace those who don't. Complex B2B sales depends on trust, judgment, and human relationship-building that AI cannot replicate. What AI can do is remove the friction, preparation, and administrative overhead that currently prevents salespeople from spending more time on those human-critical activities.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        <h3 itemprop="name">What is PA Uno?</h3>
        <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
          <p itemprop="text">PA Uno is an AI personal assistant developed by Powersales Communication that acts as a researcher, content creator, and coordinator for B2B sales professionals. It can draft emails in your tone, prepare meeting insights, summarise key accounts, and generate reports, working in parallel so you start your day reviewing what's already been done rather than doing it yourself.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

